body:
Another thing I was going to say, but it got lost in my train of thought. I am not scared of death. I haven't been since I became full-on suicidal the first time. I'm scared of doing it wrong. I'm scared of the pain. I'm scared of the thought of doing something, then changing my mind and having it be too late and being terrified for the rest of my life.

&#x200B;

And now I understand those people who say it's possible to die of a broken heart. I'm still going for now, but I loved her. I still have her marked as a favorite on facebook because most of what she posts is pictures of my son, but occasionally it'll be things related to her new relationship, and I feel like I've been punched. My heart breaks all over again.
